<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:53:38Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>US envoys fly to Russia, then Ukraine with plan 'to end war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:90649e75d63eb2ade47d6fd0ac2aa193e0c774c8ba68f994b211fd36f9e61ad3</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:53:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T10:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-fly-to-russia-then-ukraine-with-plan-to-end-war/a-79040773--b574836d4993.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-fly-to-russia-then-ukraine-with-plan-to-end-war/a-79040773?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jared Kushner and Steve Witkoff have reportedly arrived in Moscow to revive Ukraine peace talks. The trip is the pair's first visit to Kyiv since US President Donald Trump's reelection.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran war: Explosions reported near Kharg Island</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25288e2bdd4309875f68de86af7cb3a4a86a83fba301205fd72d5fcb501f1046</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-war-explosions-reported-near-kharg-island/live-79044467--182f6cf4c6d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-explosions-reported-near-kharg-island/live-79044467?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iranian media has reported that a tanker was targeted near the oil hub of Kharg Island. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: From emigration to immigration destination</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:667694ed1b15fecd6e316c50f8c846b6fb3e0e0af334f6523e4cdc6489231404</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T08:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541--ac3bd047b864.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Migration is a sensitive topic in Germany, with public debate dominated by the fear of uncontrolled immigration. But over two centuries, millions of Germans emigrated in search of a better life.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Why many Syrians feel Assad's death sentence isn't enough</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c0e857d022d7ec33b53b53b85a237c20b73000af4aa4c4de360146e7625837d</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:53:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T08:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-many-syrians-feel-assad-s-death-sentence-isn-t-enough/a-78985915--313904365f4f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-many-syrians-feel-assad-s-death-sentence-isn-t-enough/a-78985915?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In July, a Syrian court sentenced former dictator Bashar Assad to death for crimes against his own people. But after 14 years of civil war, many survivors are demanding more when it comes to transitional justice.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: 275 Indians still missing in Nepal floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53c094f769e7cc466509d949fada0e570049059a57ebcbe8bee263cccf62a4fe</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:53:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T07:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-275-indians-still-missing-in-nepal-floods/live-79043198--94765ec2f3ce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-275-indians-still-missing-in-nepal-floods/live-79043198?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Official estimates say that 275 Indians continue to be unaccounted for in Nepal's flood catastrophe. Meanwhile, no Indian travelers are said to be stranded in flood-affected Tibet. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Thousands expected at Saxony-Anhalt rallies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d5ed0ac2a752eeb42653936171a46e909629bf6351e1da9eade29d64e0854a1</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:53:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T06:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-thousands-expected-at-saxony-anhalt-rallies/live-79041302--40c4d8f77efb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-thousands-expected-at-saxony-anhalt-rallies/live-79041302?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ahead of Saxony-Anhalt's state election on Sunday, a democracy festival by civil society groups is planned in Magdeburg. The far-right AfD will also hold its final campaign rally in the state capital. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What would an AfD government in Saxony-Anhalt really mean?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be5d18e9f2dfde0ae59da78ddf7e9592132ad1c12e2a3575ec7dc0118e82e33e</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:53:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T06:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-would-an-afd-government-in-saxony-anhalt-really-mean/a-78869947--261ff10619b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-would-an-afd-government-in-saxony-anhalt-really-mean/a-78869947?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Detention centers for deportation, mandatory work for asylum-seekers, vigilante groups — the AfD wants to drastically overhaul Saxony-Anhalt. What does the party have planned?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Tunisia: Judge orders arrest of journalist Mohamed Yousfi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:885fd55030591c13b4f9fcba6f6869e91f32a8d909e98196711a995dec7dfcd2</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T03:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tunisia-judge-orders-arrest-of-journalist-mohamed-yousfi/a-79040802--a89422e15909.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tunisia-judge-orders-arrest-of-journalist-mohamed-yousfi/a-79040802?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A journalist and vocal critic of the Tunisian president, Mohamed Yousfi has been taken into custody ahead of an interview. A union called the arrest an attack on all journalists' rights.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bolivia: Deadly explosion rocks military base in Viacha</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e41e5227e7963d94b61337ec03f40f58161d87fa9e9eb40a102974cd42d41544</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T03:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bolivia-deadly-explosion-rocks-military-base-in-viacha/a-79040892--c627a7e7a20e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bolivia-deadly-explosion-rocks-military-base-in-viacha/a-79040892?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The explosion occurred at an army base where fireworks were stored. The exact cause of the blast is under investigation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UN approves world map reflecting true size of Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f5fcd5d354e093da9d8d7bf04cf63533451664f0d4f87e17447270de6854854</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T23:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/un-approves-world-map-reflecting-true-size-of-africa/a-79040629--e6486bc869d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/un-approves-world-map-reflecting-true-size-of-africa/a-79040629?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The UN General Assembly voted to adopt a map that more accurately shows the size of the continents. Only the United States voted against the measure, which projects the country as smaller than on traditional maps.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Outrage as Maltese tycoon acquitted in journalist's murder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5850e77b18851f855d0836245c8b5ed803ccd269d47f8e15578ed6b03ea5475e</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T19:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/outrage-as-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-in-journalist-s-murder/a-79027008--2a5e65f2e4f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/outrage-as-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-in-journalist-s-murder/a-79027008?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Maltese businessman Yorgen Fenech has been found not guilty of complicity to murder journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia. Almost nine years after the attack, the question of who ordered her death remains unanswered.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Fighting intensifies amid Houthi push in the west</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff1b170c8e98f87de9fab1479c6328a2706b28f14ee9d24aac00bce94e7f2512</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T19:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemen-fighting-intensifies-amid-houthi-push-in-the-west/a-79039588--651aa6fc20cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemen-fighting-intensifies-amid-houthi-push-in-the-west/a-79039588?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Houthi forces are trying to secure high ground and solidify their control of the entry to the Red Sea in the southwest. The Iran-backed militia abandoned a shaky truce with the Saudi-backed government-in-exile in July.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt: Small parties will be the kingmakers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:84480ff3443bbb7a78d8c83b7cc90e8082544d1b4ce2b8815e1239c67729ba61</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T19:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-small-parties-will-be-the-kingmakers/a-78482460--1fa346e85897.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-small-parties-will-be-the-kingmakers/a-78482460?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right AfD has good odds of winning an absolute majority in Saxony-Anhalt's parliament this state election, enabling them to govern alone. It all depends on whether other parties make the cut.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's alliance against the far right</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:717be9a098059287e1237dcde3cea7346db6afb3d1d0d0e52eaaf729006fca06</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T18:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-alliance-against-the-far-right/a-79009105--5405586db776.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-alliance-against-the-far-right/a-79009105?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Trade unions, churches and human rights activists are worried about the rise of the far-right AfD. How can civil society protect people who are threatened by far-right extremism?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria: Suspected oil thieves dead after inhaling fumes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57b495e24e3482dbdabcf7eb0fffd6b7c6a2e138eaa9766f171b2c241630c173</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-suspected-oil-thieves-dead-after-inhaling-fumes/a-79001997--76c34d7b815f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-suspected-oil-thieves-dead-after-inhaling-fumes/a-79001997?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Nigerian environmental group says that at least 37 people died trying to siphon crude oil off a ship illegally. Police acknowledged a fatal incident but gave fewer details, saying investigations continued.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany, partners aim to finalize 'return hubs' by year end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8b4d832de88c5d63ea5eb1c9c2142a455ad44e5b330e9b3ba6a13badedca586</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T14:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-partners-aim-to-finalize-return-hubs-by-year-end/a-79004242--cc966167d922.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-partners-aim-to-finalize-return-hubs-by-year-end/a-79004242?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Interior Minister Dobrindt said "technical discussions" were underway with non-EU countries to establish controversial "return hubs." Rights organizations have questioned the legality and morality of the plans.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal flood disaster puts climate justice under spotlight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:948a2a75eb8bde1d1b1f1dc74a3ab099a8a4081486ce410b7043d44b69c58e50</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-flood-disaster-puts-climate-justice-under-spotlight/a-78998617--8f177ec379f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-flood-disaster-puts-climate-justice-under-spotlight/a-78998617?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The devastating Himalayan glacial floods have raised broader questions about who should bear the costs and responsibility for the impacts of climate-related disasters.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>How can African retailers compete with Shein and Temu?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94975276f457377e7fbbdfc97f9b1ee084d91376014d69a7e05b5264d4265c53</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-can-african-retailers-compete-with-shein-and-temu/a-78988195--3bda9e77e49f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-can-african-retailers-compete-with-shein-and-temu/a-78988195?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Shein and Temu are expanding across Africa with low prices and vast product ranges. Businesses and unions warn the growth could come at a cost for local jobs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>How vulnerable is Germany's infrastructure?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5338e1d3ff59f626f85292eb712f2c436fd1cd13ce0772480f884423145a7178</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-vulnerable-is-germany-s-infrastructure/a-78990131--c453d562d3d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-vulnerable-is-germany-s-infrastructure/a-78990131?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The growing number of attacks on substations and railway lines in Germany is raising concern. Experts say that people will have to get used to the likelihood that such incidents will continue.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Romania prosecutors indict Andrew Tate for trafficking minors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d7d3ea39eef3e2dc4ec7e928f09ad073a13e249cc261ba350dabe3086eabd9ba</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T12:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/romania-prosecutors-indict-andrew-tate-for-trafficking-minors/a-78933191--81be669229d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/romania-prosecutors-indict-andrew-tate-for-trafficking-minors/a-78933191?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The social media influencer has also been indicted for money laundering and sex with a minor. His brother Tristan has been indicted for complicity.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Majority of Germans see Russia as a threat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93315f4f85165dafd1d3d479f4028a0278323b1f4d2a21cd646cca71c551ed78</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T12:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/majority-of-germans-see-russia-as-a-threat/a-78970396--5eab015b811e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/majority-of-germans-see-russia-as-a-threat/a-78970396?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than half of German citizens believe that Germany's security is threatened by Russia, according to the latest survey by public broadcaster ARD.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry></feed>
